---
description: Runtime policy modules, evaluation sets, labels and exported datasets
globs: src/doctours_reply/policies/**,src/doctours_reply/evaluation/**,eval/**,datasets/**
alwaysApply: false
---

- Policy modules start with `+++` TOML front matter holding `id` and `version`. Bump `version` on every content change, and keep `sources` pointing at packet lines.
- Policy text contains no fixture facts and no evaluation text.
- Overlays in `resources/policy_sets/` declare the `replaces_version` they expect; update it when the base module moves.
- Labels never come from expected outputs. Frozen sets (held-out, sealed) are never edited.
- Held-out runs happen only through the logged schedule, never ad hoc.
- Runtime code never imports `doctours_reply.evaluation`.
